From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] isoBuilder: build the BIOS El Torito image with the theme's
 image loaders

Since the switch from syslinux to GRUB El Torito, BIOS boots
isolinux/eltorito.img, which reads the same /boot/grub2/grub.cfg as
UEFI GRUB. That config sets the Photon theme, whose background is a PNG
and whose menu pieces are TGA images, but the image is built without
the png and tga modules and the ISO carries no /boot/grub2/i386-pc to
load them from. BIOS GRUB therefore stops before the menu with

  error: ../../grub-core/video/bitmap.c:grub_video_bitmap_load:213:
  bitmap file `/boot/grub2/themes/photon/photon.png' is of unsupported
  format.
  Press any key to continue...

and only after a timeout or a key press falls back to the plain GRUB
text menu, without the theme.

Add png and tga to the modules built into the image.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JW73JTCUGRcaNTUEQcAMtf
---
 photon_installer/isoBuilder.py | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py b/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
index 6aed7e0..8717b5a 100755
--- a/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
+++ b/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
@@ -303,7 +303,11 @@ class IsoBuilder(object):
                 f"grub2-mkimage -O i386-pc-eltorito -d /usr/lib/grub/i386-pc "
                 f"-o {self.working_dir}/isolinux/eltorito.img -p /boot/grub2 "
                 f"biosdisk iso9660 normal search search_fs_uuid search_fs_file search_label "
-                f"all_video loadenv fat ext2 gfxmenu gfxterm gfxterm_background gfxterm_menu linux probe"
+                f"all_video loadenv fat ext2 gfxmenu gfxterm gfxterm_background gfxterm_menu linux probe "
+                # the theme's background is a PNG and its menu pieces TGA
+                # images; without their loaders BIOS GRUB stops at "photon.png
+                # is of unsupported format - Press any key" before the menu
+                f"png tga"
             )
 
         if self.kickstart_path:
-- 
